{"availability":"available","full":"Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse","name":"MotionMuse","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-26T10:52:56Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:58:50Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dentarthurdent42.github.io/MotionMuse/","topics":[],"demo":"https://dentarthurdent42.github.io/MotionMuse/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:42:04.448Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:42:04.448Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:42:04.448Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:48:39.238Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T16:42:04.448Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-based instrument that maps live webcam data — hand position, gesture, and body pose — to audio synthesis parameters in real time. No plugins, no install: pure Web APIs served as static files.","Reported as \"the arpeggiator is too staccato by default\", and it was — at every setting of every control, which is the part that matters. The engine cut each arp note dead at its gate with a fade of at most 90 ms, so the run was a procession of flat-topped blocks however long the blocks were. A gate can make a note longer; it cannot give it a shape, and the difference between a note that stops and a note that rings is most of what separates an instrument from a metronome with pitches.","So the note's life is two controls now. GATE is how long it is held; SUS is how long it decays afterwards. Both are in steps, so the shape survives a tempo change: an arpeggio that rings a half-step under the next note keeps doing that at 2/s and at 20/s."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"57f2b085aceeabc5defb1fe1feef2f57b40b740506cdb2289f139e305f54d638","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:39.414Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:25:23.247Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A browser-based instrument that maps live webcam data — hand position, gesture, and body pose — to audio synthesis parameters in real time. No plugins, no install: pure Web APIs served as static files.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Point a phone at it and the app opens configured the same way — the point being that handing someone a patch should not require a file, an account or a server.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"It is, but only when a second hand is actually in frame: with one hand up, asking for two costs exactly the same, because the palm detector finds one hand and the landmark model runs once.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Guidance: lite for mobile / low-power (lowest latency), full when a desktop GPU can afford 2× lite's cost for tighter tracking, heavy only when accuracy is critical and latency isn't, MoveNet Lightning as the low-latency alternative if its jitter score wins on your device.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"57f2b085aceeabc5defb1fe1feef2f57b40b740506cdb2289f139e305f54d638","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:25:23.249Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T23:58:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dentarthurdent42/MotionMuse/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:25:23.257Z","hash":"57f2b085aceeabc5defb1fe1feef2f57b40b740506cdb2289f139e305f54d638","originalBytes":198325,"storedBytes":198325,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["one","hand","every","which","node","chord","what","same"